WEBVTT

00:22:57.713 --> 00:23:00.390
Transitions: when somebody moves in,
you welcome them in.

00:23:00.414 --> 00:23:01.939
If somebody comes out of prison,

00:23:01.963 --> 00:23:04.679
you have a ritual to welcome them
back into the community.

00:23:04.703 --> 00:23:08.056
And we've sort of let that all strip away
in our desire for, basically,

00:23:08.080 --> 00:23:09.898
accomplishment, because we're so busy,

00:23:09.922 --> 00:23:12.323
and our desire to put privacy
over everything else.

00:23:12.347 --> 00:23:14.158
CA: So, those are the drivers of that?

00:23:14.182 --> 00:23:15.722
That just we raised a generation

00:23:15.746 --> 00:23:18.232
to believe that they
should be focused internally

00:23:18.256 --> 00:23:20.982
on their own needs,
passions and potentials

00:23:21.006 --> 00:23:25.633
and just didn't encourage
old-fashioned but beautiful ideas

00:23:25.657 --> 00:23:28.449
like, "Just show up.
Be there for so-and-so.

00:23:28.473 --> 00:23:30.815
Stop talking about yourself so much."